===Etymology 1===
1655, from {{bor|en|fr|gril}}, from {{der|en|frm}}, from {{der|en|fro|greïl}}, {{m|fro|graïl||gridiron}}, from {{m|fro|graïlle||grate, grating}}, from {{der|en|la|crātīcula||gridiron}}, diminutive of {{m|la|crātis||hurdle, wickerwork}}, q.v. Related to {{m|en|griddle}}, {{m|en|hurdle}}.

====Alternative forms====
{{wikipedia|grille|grille}}
* {{l|en|grille}} {{qual|only in sense of "grating"}}

====Noun====
[[Image:Brazier.JPG|thumb|[[brazier|Brazier]] with '''grill''' and pot rest]]
{{en-noun}}

# A [[grating]]; a [[grid]] of [[wire]] or a sheet of material with a pattern of holes or slots, usually used to [[protect]] something while allowing the passage of [[air]] and [[liquid]]s. Typical uses: to allow air through a [[fan]] while preventing fingers or objects from passing; to allow people to talk to somebody, while preventing [[attack]].
#* {{RQ:Chmbrs YngrSt|I}}
#*: The house was a big elaborate limestone affair, evidently new. Winter sunshine sparkled on lace-hung casement, on glass marquise, and the burnished bronze foliations of '''grille''' and door.
# On a [[vehicle]], a [[slot]]ted cover as above, to protect and hide the [[radiator]], while admitting air to cool it.
# {{lb|en|UK}} A cooking device comprising a source of [[radiative]] [[heat]] and a means of holding food under it; a [[broiler]] in US English
# {{lb|en|US}} A cooking device comprising a source of radiative and [[convective]] heat and a means of holding food above it; a [[barbecue]].
#: {{ux|en|I put some peppers and mushrooms on the '''grill''' to go with dinner.}}
# Food (designed to be) cooked on a grill.
#: {{ux|en|a packet of frozen cauliflower cheese '''grills'''}}
# A [[grillroom]]; a [[restaurant]] serving grilled food. <!--in Webster 1913-->
#: {{ux|en|These coupons will get you a discount at Johnny's Bar and '''Grill'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1986|work=New York|volume=19|section=part 5|page=385|passage=Everyone's meeting at the new '''grill''' in town! And everyone's having a real good time! They're drinking frozen blue Margaritas. Munching on Cajun popcorn shrimp. Laughing with old friends and getting to know new ones.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} A type of jewelry worn on the front teeth.
#: {{synonyms|en|fronts|golds}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial|by extension}} The front teeth regarded collectively.
# {{lb|en|internet slang|humorous}} {{misspelling of|en|girl}} <!--needs moving to separate etymology section-->
#: {{ux|en|r u a '''grill'''?}}

