====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cook]] (food) on a grill; to [[barbecue]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:cook}}
#: {{ux|en|Why don't we get together Saturday and '''grill''' some burgers?}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|Australian|NZ|UK}} To cook food under the [[element]] of a [[stove]] or only under the top element of an [[oven]] – {{lb|en|US}} [[broil]], {{lb|en|cooking}} [[salamander]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|colloquial}} To [[interrogate]]; to [[question]] [[aggressively]] or [[harshly]].
#: {{ux|en|The police '''grilled''' him about his movements at the time of the crime.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|informal}} To feel very hot; to [[swelter]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1898|title=The Day's Work|author=Rudyard Kipling|passage=He had '''grilled''' in the heat, sweated in the rains, and shivered with fever under the rude thatch roof; {{...}} }}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[stamp]] or [[mark]] with a grill.

